Chart Grabber core
==================

Licence of this program: GPL-3.0-or-later. The full text is in the file LICENSE next to this one. The source code is in the
repository this package was built from; the version and the commit are printed by `chart-grabber-cli --version`.

Source code: https://github.com/Sea-For-Friends/chart-grabber-cli tag v2026.10.11
Source code of the third-party packages (MSYS2): https://repo.msys2.org/mingw/sources/ (source archives named
mingw-w64-<name>-<version>.src.tar.zst) and https://packages.msys2.org/packages/mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-<name> (page of each package).

This file lists the third-party components that the Windows zip (chart-grabber-cli-<version>-win64.zip) carries. All of them are
unmodified binaries of the MSYS2 UCRT64 repository (https://www.msys2.org/, packages mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-<name>); the source of
every package is linked from its page at https://packages.msys2.org/ and is built from the recipes in
https://github.com/msys2/MINGW-packages. The licence text of each component is in licenses\<name>\ of the zip.
Where MSYS2 ships no licence file for a package (libidn2, lz4), licenses\<name>\ holds the upstream texts: licenses\lz4\ has
LICENSE (lz4 v1.10.0, programs: GPL-2.0-or-later) and lib-LICENSE (the library, BSD-2-Clause); licenses\libidn2\ has COPYING (GPL-3.0, the base text of LGPL-3.0),
COPYING.LESSERv3 (LGPL-3.0) and COPYING.unicode (libidn2 v2.3.8).

Qt (LGPL-3.0-only)
------------------
The zip links Qt 6 (Qt6Core.dll, Qt6Gui.dll, Qt6Network.dll, Qt6Qml.dll) and loads its plugins (platforms\, imageformats\, tls\) dynamically.
The Qt libraries are used under the GNU Lesser General Public Licence version 3 (licenses\qt6-base\LGPL-3.0-only.txt, with the
GPL-3.0 text next to it). You may replace them with your own build of Qt that has the same minor version (6.12): stop the
program, put your Qt6Core.dll, Qt6Gui.dll, Qt6Network.dll, Qt6Qml.dll (and the Qt6Qml*.dll it needs) and the plugin DLLs into this folder (the folders platforms, imageformats
and tls) over the shipped ones, and start chart-grabber-cli.exe again; nothing is linked statically and nothing checks the files.
The Qt source is available from https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/ and from the MSYS2 package source named above.

Linux packages
--------------
The Linux .deb packages carry no copy of these components: they depend on the libraries of the Debian or Ubuntu release, and those
packages ship their own copyright files (/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright). Nothing is listed here for them.

Components of the Windows zip
-----------------------------
One row per MSYS2 package: name | version | licence (SPDX expression, from the package metadata) | upstream URL.
The check tools/vm/notice_check.sh fails the build of the zip when a DLL belongs to a package that has no row, when a version
differs from the one in tools/vm/manifests/win10.txt, or when licenses\<name>\ is missing.

